<title>USA: FMR group cuts Continental Airlines stake.</title>
<headline>FMR group cuts Continental Airlines stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by FMR Corp, the parent of the investment firm to Fidelity Funds, said Wesnesday it reduced its stake in Continental Airlines Inc to 12.02 percent or 5,754,260 class B common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Comission, the group said it sold a net of 645,200 shares between August 13 and September 16 at prices ranging from $21.54 to $25.00 a share.</p>
</text>
